# Planning in Copilot

Respect the session's active mode. Native plan mode is a host/user control, not a
dedicated planning tool exposed to the skill.
In native plan mode, explore and draft in the host's private planning workspace.
Do not write project artifacts until that mode permits implementation. Approval
of a plan and persistence into the workflow's project plan path are separate steps.
Never select plan-then-autopilot or bypass approval on the developer's behalf.

In an authorized standard session, prepare the workflow's reviewable plan and
preserve its explicit sign-off gates. Updating stage progress does not switch modes.
Bootstrap's already-authorized deterministic installation does not require entering
plan mode. A copied template is not a completed installation.
